## Coding rules to remember while working
- Strict TDD: failing test first, then implementation. Canonical
  commands in CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md.
- Root-cause fixes only. No shims, no monkey-patches, no fallback
  systems. Old saves are disposable.
- Each phase boundary leaves the game runnable/savable/loadable.
- Substrate-then-sweep migration model (per PROJ-431/436): new seam
  first, callers sweep next, final cutover deletes the old shape.
- Update docs in the same change when behavior, architecture, workflow,
  or conventions move (Rule 2 in CLAUDE.md).
- Never read or write docs/_ignore/.
- No worktrees per user standing preference. Serial in the main
  checkout.
- Public functions/methods require return-type annotations using
  modern syntax (int | None, dict[str, X]).
- Production files under game/ stay under 500 LOC; split by
  responsibility when a touched file approaches that ceiling.
- Broad `except Exception` requires intentional-reason comment.

